.git
# NXP Code Signing Tool: never in the tree or the image (.gitignore and
# scripts/check-tracked-cst.sh). Everything inside any cst-* directory, at any
# depth and whatever its suffix, stays out. Docker cleans a trailing slash
# away, so `**/cst-*/` would mean `**/cst-*` and drop scripts/cst-check.sh as
# well; `/**` matches only what lies inside such a directory.
**/cst-*/**
**/cst-*.tgz
# The pinned tools make tools installs outside the image
.tools/
# The vendor images .gitignore keeps out of the tree (and so out of
# scripts/image-tag.sh's hash) stay out of the image too; the test in
# test/ci_scripts_test.sh holds every resources/ rule of .gitignore here.
resources/*yocto*.zip
resources/ucm-imx95:yocto-linux/
